<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Pahlavi Iran</h1><p class="st-meta">1925 CE – 1979 CE · capital Tehran</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Iranian monarchy, under Reza Shah and his son Mohammad Reza Shah, which pursued rapid modernisation until overthrown by the revolution of 1979.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reza-shah">Reza Khan</a>, an officer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-cossack-brigade">Persian Cossack Brigade</a>, seized power in a coup in 1921 and became prime minister in 1923. In 1925 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-consultative-assembly">Majlis</a> deposed the last ruler of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/qajar-iran">Qajar Iran</a>, and Reza Khan was crowned Reza Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-persian">Pahlavi</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reza-shah">Reza Shah</a> built a centralised state with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conscription">conscript</a> army, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trans-iranian-railway">Trans-Iranian Railway</a> (completed 1938), the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-tehran">University of Tehran</a> and secular law, banned the women's veil in 1936 and asked foreign states to call the country <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from 1935. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-soviet-invasion-of-iran">Anglo-Soviet invasion</a> of 1941 forced his abdication in favour of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-reza-pahlavi">Mohammad Reza Shah</a>. Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-mosaddegh">Mohammad Mosaddegh</a> nationalised oil in 1951 but was overthrown in a 1953 coup backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-intelligence-agency">CIA</a> and MI6. The shah's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-revolution">White Revolution</a> of 1963 brought land reform and women's suffrage, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savak">SAVAK</a> secret police suppressed opponents.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">Inflation</a>, repression and religious opposition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhollah-khomeini">Ayatollah Khomeini</a> produced mass protests in 1978. The shah left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in January 1979, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-iran">Islamic Republic of Iran</a> was proclaimed that April.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/pahlavi-iran.jpg" alt="Pahlavi Iran" width="320" height="183"><figcaption>Image: Original emblem: Government of Iran (1970s) Vectorization and manual modifications by Shfarshid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Iran_with_Official_Lion_and_Sun_emblem_stylized_1970s.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1925 CE – 1979 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tehran</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Reza Shah, Mohammad Reza Shah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Twelver Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Imperial State of Iran, Pahlavi dynasty, Imperial Iran</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=pahlavi-iran" aria-label="Pahlavi Iran on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5978 888 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Pahlavi Iran lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6298 1144L6099 1026M6298 1144L6298 1144M6298 1144L6298 1144M6298 1144L6153 1065M6298 1144L6148 1109"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6099 1026h0M6298 1144h0M6298 1144h0M6153 1065h0M6148 1109h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6298 1144h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6298 1144h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tehran. <a href="/atlas?year=1952&amp;focus=pahlavi-iran">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
